;; opens the editor straight into the vendored 2D platformer demo (../godot-demo — the payload
;; dir beside this one; cwd = this app dir, so the spec works from any root) — wow-on-open
;; instead of an empty Project Manager. The driver is pinned because the V3D cannot do the
;; Forward+/Clustered tier (<48 textures/stage); opengl3 is the pin, not Vulkan Mobile, because
;; under Vulkan the editor deadlocks in V3D's swapchain teardown and never closes. It is also
;; what the demo asks for — project.godot declares gl_compatibility, and the game the editor
;; runs already uses it. The rootfs seeds use_native_file_dialogs: Godot takes its Open/Save
;; dialogs to the portal (the ujima picker) only when sandboxed or so told.
{:kind :exec :label "Godot" :category :code
 :exec ["./godot" "--editor" "--path" "../godot-demo"
        "--rendering-driver" "opengl3"]
 :window {:class "Godot"}}  ; res_class, xprop-verified
